Seed is deterministically rebuilt at Docker build time from the tracked
source_data/ snapshots by `PYTHONHASHSEED=0 python3 seed_data.py` (its
__main__ block bootstraps the app engine, writes instance/statista.db and
freezes a byte-identical copy as instance_seed/statista.db — the same
contract as the mta / imgur / instructure build-generated seeds). The
instance_seed/ directory is therefore NOT part of the HF asset bundle and
is wiped by the Dockerfile stanza before the rebuild; only static media
ships in the tarball.

The rebuild is byte-deterministic on one SQLite build (not just
digest-deterministic): the statistics indexes are created by a
fixed-order after_create hook in app.py instead of model-declared
Index() entries, because SQLAlchemy's create_all() iterates
Table.indexes — a set whose order follows ASLR-dependent object hashes.
Verifiers pin the logical schema digest e3571669… and rows digest
aa83591b… (inquiries table included; regional chart 256626 recovered;
conversion-rate statistic 439576 stores its country table). A host
md5 can differ across SQLite versions and is not the contract.
